course: dictionary
lesson: 9855
title: Symbols and what they stand for
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A symbol is a sign, shape or picture that stands for something else. Think of a red heart: it is not really a heart in your chest, it stands for love. The clue is in the word stands. It is standing in for a bigger idea.
explain: Some symbols are objects or ideas that stand for something bigger. «In 1936 Turing described an imaginary machine with a tape, a head that reads and writes symbols, and rules.» Here symbols are the marks the machine reads and writes, so the word means signs with meaning. When you meet symbol, ask: what does this stand for?
explain: Maths and science are full of symbols. In «+ means add», the plus sign is a symbol, and in science «O» is the short letter name for oxygen. You do not need to guess these. Learn what each one stands for, and check a key or a table when you are unsure.
fact: A symbol is a sign, shape or picture that stands for something else.
fact: «The beaver became a symbol of Canada» because beaver fur was so valuable.
fact: In science, a chemical symbol is a short letter name for an element: O for oxygen, H for hydrogen, Fe for iron.
fact: On a map, a map key explains the symbols: a cross can stand for a church, and blue lines can stand for rivers.
fact: Warning symbols show danger: a skull means poison, a flame means flammable, and a lightning bolt means electricity.
exercise: A red heart is a symbol. What does it stand for? | A cold day | A broken window | *Love | Fast running
exercise: In science, «O» is the chemical symbol. What does O stand for? | *Oxygen | Ocean | Orange | Owl
exercise: Which picture is a warning symbol for poison? | *A skull | A green tree | A blue wave | A smiling sun
test: On a map, what is a map key for? | To tell you the time of day | To show how old the map is | *To explain what the symbols on the map mean | To count the number of roads
test: «The red poppy with a black centre» is a symbol for remembering the dead. What does the word symbol mean? | *A sign, shape or picture that stands for something else | Something that is very loud | A kind of plant that grows only in winter | A number that you add
exam: «The beaver became a symbol of Canada» because beaver fur was valuable; a symbol is best described as | *A sign or picture that stands for something bigger | A heavy animal that lives in lakes | A word that means the same as beaver | A coin used for trade
